 "stimulus_html": "Perform the following operations without a calculator. Simplify if possible.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 505360,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"\\left( {1.2\\sqrt {21} } \\right) \\times \\left( {4.5\\sqrt {14} } \\right)\">\\left( {1.2\\sqrt {21} } \\right) \\times \\left( {4.5\\sqrt {14} } \\right)</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"1.2\\sqrt {21}  \\times \\left( {4.5\\sqrt {14} } \\right)\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 1: Multiply the rational part.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"1.2 \\times 4.5 = 5.4\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: If necessary, reduce the result of Step 1 to lowest terms.</p>\n<p>Not necessary.</p>\n<p>Step 3: Multiply the irrational parts.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\sqrt {21}  \\times {\\rm{ }}\\sqrt {14} {\\rm{ }} = {\\rm{ }}\\sqrt {294} \"></span></p>\n<p>Step 4: If necessary, reduce the result from Step 3 to lowest terms.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\sqrt {294}  = \\sqrt {49} \\sqrt 6  = 7\\sqrt 6 \"></span></p>\n<p>Step 5: The result is the product of the rational and the irrational parts.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"5.4\\left( {7\\sqrt 6 } \\right) = 37.8\\sqrt 6 \"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"37.8\\sqrt 6\">37.8\\sqrt 6</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 505361,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"38\\pi  \\div \\left(2\\pi \\right)\">38\\pi  \\div 2\\pi</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"38\\pi  \\div \\left( {2\\pi } \\right)\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 1: Divide the rational part.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"38 \\div 2 = 19\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: If necessary, reduce the result of Step 1 to lowest terms.</p>\n<p>Not necessary.</p>\n<p>Step 3: Divide the irrational parts.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\pi  \\div \\pi  = 1\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 4: If necessary, reduce the result from Step 3 to lowest terms.</p>\n<p>Not necessary.</p>\n<p>Step 5: The result is the product of the rational and the irrational parts.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"19 \\times 1 = 19\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "19"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
